  "reason": "The best result so far is config_031 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, acc 0.678). The scvi_n200 RNA encoder provided a substantial boost over pca_n2000 (0.678 vs 0.639), indicating learned representations matter. The image encoder comparison with pca_n2000 showed resnet50 ≈ imagenet_vit_l (0.639 vs 0.635), but that was with a linear PCA representation. With scvi_n200 (a learned, nonlinear encoder), the interaction with a more expressive image encoder (ViT-L) could differ, potentially capturing complementary spatial-structural features. Config_037 is a clean single-variable swap (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) from the current best, making it the most logical exploitation step. As the final experiment, it directly tests whether we can push past 0.678 by upgrading the image backbone while keeping all other proven-optimal settings (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion, scvi_n200) fixed."
